<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William of Champlitte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1209</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William of Champlitte was a Burgundian knight who took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>. In 1205, with Geoffrey of Villehardouin, he conquered the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> and became the first Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>. In 1208 he left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> to claim an inheritance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> and died on the journey in 1209, after which Geoffrey took over the principality.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-of-champlitte.jpg" alt="William of Champlitte" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_famille_de_Champlitte.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
